meta {
  name: List Outgoing Requests
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.listRecords?repo={{did}}&collection=app.bsky.graph.followRequest&limit=50
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  repo: {{did}}
  collection: app.bsky.graph.followRequest
  limit: 50
}

docs {
  # List Outgoing Requests
  
  Lists follow request records you have created (outgoing requests).
  
  ## Query Parameters
  - `repo` (string): Your DID
  - `collection` (string): "app.bsky.graph.followRequest"
  - `limit` (number, optional): Maximum number of results (default: 50)
  - `cursor` (string, optional): Pagination cursor
  
  ## Response
  Returns a list of your follow request records:
  ```json
  {
    "records": [
      {
        "uri": "at://did:plc:your-did/app.bsky.graph.followRequest/xxx",
        "cid": "...",
        "value": {
          "$type": "app.bsky.graph.followRequest",
          "subject": "did:plc:alice-did",
          "status": "pending",
          "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
        }
      }
    ],
    "cursor": "..."
  }
  ```
  
  **Note:** You can filter the results by status in your application code.
  
  ## Test Scenario
  Used to check status of sent requests:
  1. Bob authenticates
  2. Bob creates follow request to Alice (private profile)
  3. Bob lists his follow request records
  4. Verify request to Alice appears with status "pending"
  5. Bob can check later to see if status changed to "approved" or "denied"
  
  **Common Use Case:** Show a list of pending outgoing requests in the UI so the user can track their status.
}
